Package: kde-config-sonic-screenlocker
Architecture: any
Depends: libsonicscreenlocker6 (= ${binary:Version}),
         systemsettings,
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
Breaks: kde-config-kscreenlocker,
Provides: kde-config-kscreenlocker,
Description: KCM Module for sonic-screenlocker
 Sonic DE systemsettings module to configure sonic-screenlocker.
 .
 sonic-screenlocker can be configured to support the PAM ("Pluggable Authentication
 Modules") system for password checking (for unlocking the display).
 .
 PAM is a flexible application-transparent configurable user-authentication
 system found on FreeBSD, Solaris, and Linux (and maybe other unixes).
 .
 Information about PAM may be found on its homepage
       http://www.kernel.org/pub/linux/libs/pam/
 (Despite the location, this information is NOT Linux-specific.)
 .
 This package contains the KCM settings module for sonic-screenlocker.

